            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "Are you sure, the null object is because of that warning? I would suppose the serializable problem should be logged as an error if it was truly critical...",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443"
            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2009-01-20T20:43:51.978+0000",
          "updated": "2009-01-20T20:43:51.978+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12412858/comment/12665592",
          "id": "12665592",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=michael.xue",
            "name": "michael.xue",
            "key": "michael.xue",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Xue",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Yes, I'm.   The jackrabbit entry in weblogic JNDI tree is not populated with 'org.apache.jackrabbit.jca.JCAResourceAdapter' at all, showing a red ! instead.  Originally I deployed the same jackrabbit-jca.rar in the dev server, which is single (non-cluster) server environment.  Everything worked great.   However, as soon as I moved to the cluster environment, JCAResourceAdapter just couldn't fit.   Yes, I agree, JCAResourceAdapter must implement Serializable.  Otherwise, it won't be deployable in any cluster environment.     ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=michael.xue",
            "name": "michael.xue",
            "key": "michael.xue",
            "avatarUrls": {
